    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can you give me a quick summary of the mandatory steps a company has to follow when a user submits a formal \"right to be forgotten\" request under gdpr? i need to outline the process for an internal memo.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under GDPR, a company must follow these mandatory steps upon receiving a \"right to be forgotten\" request:\n\n1. Respond promptly: Acknowledge the request within one month, extending additional time if necessary.\n2. Assess the request: Verify that the request is valid under GDPR and that the processing of the data is irrelevant to the user's purpose.\n3. Erase personal data: Upon validation, proceed to delete all personal data linked to the user, including backups, unless prohibited by legal requirements.\n4. Notify interested parties: Inform any third-party processors, in writing, to likewise erase the relevant personal data.\n5. Confirm completion: Provide the user with confirmation that their data has been erased, or explain the reasons if any legal exception applies.\n\nThese steps ensure a timely, precise, and full compliance with the GDPR's right to be forgotten.",
